        a       ecrm:E53_Place .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/464877bd-6eb8-3f4d-a40f-36a933c8b45b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in darning stitch, over two and under two threads, backed and faced with plain weave glazed cotton.\nEmbroidery threads: 2S silk; black, white, yellow, light blue, pink [faded], light pink, light brown, light green.\nLoosely woven cotton fabric forming the background to the coloured embroidery.  Small geometric motifs combined to form a diamond grid.  The largest motif is a 4-pointed star, either brown with an inner yellow star and central blue diamond or green, brown and yellow.  These motifs alternate in off-set rows.  In between are pairs of small pink diamonds and a white and black square. The squares and pink diamonds form the grid and the stars fill the diamond shaped spaces.\nThere is a border formed by repeating part of the main pattern.\nBacking: blue glazed cotton.\nFacing: bias-cut, blue glazed cotton."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/464877bd-6eb8-3f4d-a40f-36a933c8b45b> .

