        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, packed design of overlapping crosses and squares, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1770-1830"@en , "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in darning stitch, over two and under two threads, backed and faced with plain weave glazed cotton.\nEmbroidery threads: 2S silk; black, white, yellow, light blue, pink [faded], light pink, light brown, light green.\nLoosely woven cotton fabric forming the background to the coloured embroidery.  Small geometric motifs combined to form a diamond grid.  The largest motif is a 4-pointed star, either brown with an inner yellow star and central blue diamond or green, brown and yellow.  These motifs alternate in off-set rows.  In between are pairs of small pink diamonds and a white and black square. The squares and pink diamonds form the grid and the stars fill the diamond shaped spaces.\nThere is a border formed by repeating part of the main pattern.\nBacking: blue glazed cotton.\nFacing: bias-cut, blue glazed cotton."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/68983b37-e715-3b77-9dcc-2319dacf7d3a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/5c2279a1-902a-3ebf-aa81-24e45a4a3a51> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/29c28481-cf8e-3a4d-9d2f-66963c8930fd> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in darning stitch, over two and under two threads, backed and faced with plain weave glazed cotton.\nEmbroidery threads: 2S silk; black, white, yellow, light blue, pink [faded], light pink, light brown, light green.\nLoosely woven cotton fabric forming the background to the coloured embroidery.  Small geometric motifs combined to form a diamond grid.  The largest motif is a 4-pointed star, either brown with an inner yellow star and central blue diamond or green, brown and yellow.  These motifs alternate in off-set rows.  In between are pairs of small pink diamonds and a white and black square. The squares and pink diamonds form the grid and the stars fill the diamond shaped spaces.\nThere is a border formed by repeating part of the main pattern.\nBacking: blue glazed cotton.\nFacing: bias-cut, blue glazed cotton."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, packed design of overlapping crosses and squares, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1770-1830"@en ;
